{"annotations":{"readOnlyHint":true},"description":"Read one parsed section body. The body runs from after the heading to the next heading at the same or a higher level, so it includes nested subsections, and the last section runs to the end of its file, including \\end{document} when the file holds it. By default this reads a single file. With followIncludes: true, filePath is the document get_sections started from and sectionId comes from that call; a section that lies in one file is read as that file holds it, include directives included, which is exactly what write_section replaces, and revision is that file's revision; a section in an included file ends where that file ends, so it never holds the including file's \\end{document}. A section with spansFiles: true reads as flattened text across files, for reading only.","inputSchema":{"$schema":"https://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/schema","properties":{"filePath":{"description":"Project-relative path using forward slashes","minLength":1,"type":"string"},"followIncludes":{"default":false,"description":"Follow \\input, \\include, \\subfile, and \\import directives from filePath down, as get_full_document does; defaults to false, one file only","type":"boolean"},"projectId":{"description":"Overleaf project ID","minLength":1,"type":"string"},"sectionId":{"minLength":1,"type":"string"}},"required":["projectId","filePath","sectionId"],"type":"object"},"name":"get_section_content","outputSchema":{"$schema":"https://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/schema","additionalProperties":false,"properties":{"content":{"type":"string"},"revision":{"type":"string"},"section":{"anyOf":[{"additionalProperties":false,"properties":{"bodyStart":{"maximum":9007199254740991,"minimum":0,"type":"integer"},"command":{"enum":["part","chapter","section","subsection","subsubsection","paragraph","subparagraph"],"type":"string"},"end":{"maximum":9007199254740991,"minimum":0,"type":"integer"},"filePath":{"type":"string"},"headingEnd":{"maximum":9007